{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789259554,"nonce":"TiFCSzeOckw1FbK2qmAg24jipp8=","title":"ZynML's prelude, tensor and simd modules ship lowered","message":"The snapshot format carries a module's HIR (c43c507) and the Python\nlibrary uses it; ZynML's build script still writes its three modules\nparsed only, so every ZynML compile lowers whatever of them it reaches.\n\nBlocker: zynml/build.rs builds zyntax_embed parse-only and has no ZRTL\nplugin signatures, and `inject_builtin_externs` skips every builtin\nalias without a signature, so the prelude cannot lower on its own (its\ncalls to println and friends have nothing to land on). Options: the\nbuild script links the static plugins zynml already links and reads\ntheir signatures through `static_plugin()`; or the grammar's @builtin\nsection carries the extern types so no signature is needed. The second\nis also what a wasm build wants.\n\nThen: lower prelude first, tensor with prelude as a prelowered\ndependency (`lower_for_snapshot(.., prelowered)`), simd likewise;\n`module_lowered` for each. Generic templates stay in the HIR and\nmonomorphise from user call sites. Check `stdlib_cost` before and\nafter.","files":null}]}